    "result_text": "The suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). Here's the situation, reported honestly.\n\n## Finding: the change is already satisfied in the codebase\n\nEvery rejection path (400, 409, 429) already returns an RFC7807 `application/problem+json` body with `type`, `title`, `status`, and `detail`. I verified this rather than assuming:\n\n- **Mechanism** \u2014 All escalation handlers route through one shared helper, `rest/escalation/ProblemDetails.build(...)`, which builds a Spring `ProblemDetail` (sets `type=about:blank`, `title`, `detail`, and `status` via `forStatus`). Each handler sends it as `ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail>>`, which serializes with the `application/problem+json` content type.\n- **Coverage of the required statuses**:\n  - **400** \u2014 `ValidationExceptionHandler`, `AddressRequired`, `DisposableEmail`, `InvalidPostcode`, `InvalidTelephone`, `FutureRegistrationDate`\n  - **409** \u2014 `DuplicateEmail`, `DuplicateTelephone`, `DuplicateHousehold`, `DuplicateIdentity`, `CityAtCapacity`\n  - **429** \u2014 `DailyOwnerLimit`\n- **Verified emitted body** (throwaway test, since `AcceptanceTest` only asserts `$.status`):\n  ```json\n  {\"detail\":\"The request contains invalid or missing parameters\",\"status\":400,\n   \"title\":\"MethodArgumentNotValidException\",\"type\":\"about:blank\", ...}\n  ```\n  All four members present; status codes unchanged.\n\n**Tests:** the new `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectionIsProblemJson` (asserts `contentTypeCompatibleWith(\"application/problem+json\")` and `$.status == 400`) passes, and the full `mvn test` run is `BUILD SUCCESS` with no failures.\n\n**Structural impact:** zero \u2014 no source files needed changing. The existing design already isolates the RFC7807 concern in the small `ProblemDetails` helper plus thin per-exception handlers, which is exactly the low-WMC, small-cohesive-unit shape the task calls for. I made no production edits (the only file I created, a scratch verification test, has been removed).\n\nIf you expected the repo to start from a pre-change state, note that the handlers on disk already implement this \u2014 so nothing further is required for the spec and tests to pass.",
